{"declarations":[{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">def</span>\n<span class=\"decl_name\"><a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./Init/LetFun.html#letFun\"><span class=\"name\">letFun</span></a></span><span class=\"impl_arg\"><span class=\"decl_args\">\n<span class=\"fn\">{<span class=\"fn\">α</span> : <a href=\"./foundational_types.html\">Sort</a> u}</span></span>\n</span><span class=\"impl_arg\"><span class=\"decl_args\">\n<span class=\"fn\">{<span class=\"fn\">β</span> : <span class=\"fn\"><span class=\"fn\">α</span> → <a href=\"./foundational_types.html\">Sort</a> v</span>}</span></span>\n</span><span class=\"decl_args\">\n<span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">v</span> : <span class=\"fn\">α</span>)</span></span>\n<span class=\"decl_args\">\n<span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">f</span> : <span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">x</span> : <span class=\"fn\">α</span>) → <span class=\"fn\"><span class=\"fn\">β</span> <span class=\"fn\">x</span></span></span>)</span></span>\n<span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><span class=\"fn\"><span class=\"fn\">β</span> <span class=\"fn\">v</span></span></div></div>","info":{"doc":"`letFun v (fun x => b)` is a function version of `have x := v; b`.\nThis is equal to `(fun x => b) v`, so the value of `x` is not accessible to `b`.\nThis is in contrast to `let x := v; b`, where the value of `x` is accessible to `b`.\n\nThis used to be the way `have`/`let_fun` syntax was encoded,\nand there used to be special support for `letFun` in WHNF and `simp`.\n","docLink":"./Init/LetFun.html#letFun","kind":"def","line":12,"name":"letFun","sourceLink":"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/blob/6a10ac8c22beadecabdbb0919c2b50214762f91d/src/Init/LetFun.lean#L12-L21"}}],"imports":["Init.Notation"],"instances":[],"name":"Init.LetFun"}